- rule_id: SOR007
  rule_name: unprotected-initialize
  severity: error
  message: "initializer `initialize` writes storage but has neither an already-initialized guard nor a `require_auth` call; it can be called by anyone or called twice"
  file: tests/fixtures/vulnerable/sor007_unprotected_init.rs
  line: 21
  column: 12
  help: "add `if env.storage().instance().has(&DataKey::Admin) { return Err(Error::AlreadyInitialized); }` and/or `admin.require_auth()` at the start of the function"
  docs_url: "https://github.com/Mossad-esc/soroban-lint/blob/main/docs/rules/SOR007.md"
